From 5af1afecfe38fecc81fad68ff74f944b6a706a5c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 17:34:26 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08154/11362] [outer-loop] exp6091 harness: pin the generator
 substrate and prove it per cell

--parallel 1 (llama-server defaults to 4 slots on a unified KV cache, so one
slot gets n_ctx/4 -- the slot arithmetic _default_induce_n_ctx documents);
server stdout/stderr to a FILE not DEVNULL; substrate_witness() reads the exe
path and loaded shared objects of whatever PID owns the port, before AND after
every cell, because a HIP build on the iGPU and a CUDA build on a 3090 both
answer /health 200 and both generate correct text. A cell whose server died
mid-cell is RECORDED and marked substrate_cuda_throughout=false, then excluded;
a HIP build taking the port aborts the run.

No shipped default is flipped; results/arc_e3 is never written.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JntPrUGLNesPcJH1pyfFYw
